// Unit tests under `src/`, which no other project covers.
//
// `tsconfig.app.json` excludes `**/*.test.*` and `tsconfig.node.json` includes
// only the config files and `tests/**` (Playwright + agentic). That leaves
// every `src/**/*.test.tsx` typechecked by nothing at all — vitest transpiles
// without checking — so even now that `lint:ts` really runs, it cannot catch a
// TS2304 or TS2345 in a test file. That is not theoretical: renaming one hook
// field in this PR left three test files passing a prop that no longer
// existed, and every one of them still went green.
//
// NOT in `tsconfig.json`'s `references`, deliberately. Turning it on today
// surfaces 118 pre-existing errors across 21 files — mostly fixtures missing
// fields the wire types have since grown — and a referenced project that fails
// would break the pre-commit gate for every contributor. Run it directly:
//
//     pnpm lint:ts:tests
//
// Clearing that backlog and adding the reference is the follow-up; every test
// file under `src/pages/ide/MetricTree/` is already clean, so the count only
// goes down from here.
//
// Same compiler options as the app: a test that type-checks under looser rules
// than the code it exercises is not testing the same types.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.app.json",
  // `src/test-setup.ts` must be in the program, not merely on disk: its
  // `@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest` import is what augments vitest's
  // `Assertion` with `toBeInTheDocument` and friends. Without it every such
  // matcher is a TS2339.
  //
  // No `types` override — an explicit array turns OFF automatic @types
  // inclusion, which drops `vite/client` and takes the app's own sources down
  // with it (`?worker` imports, `react-markdown`).
  "include": [
    // Ambient declarations (`src/types/*.d.ts`). `tsconfig.app.json` gets these
    // for free by including all of `src`; a project that lists only test files
    // does not, and their absence invents errors in the app's own sources —
    // `react-markdown.d.ts` alone accounted for 22 of them.
    "src/**/*.d.ts",
    "src/test-setup.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.tsx",
    "src/**/__tests__/**/*"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
